            <ArticleTitle>Use of opioids in non-cancer pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>459-63</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The use of opioids for chronic pain of non-malignant origin remains controversial. However, problems anticipated from experience with animal experiments and pain-free abusers seldom cause difficulties when opioids are used appropriately to treat pain. With sensible guidelines, and in the context of a multidisciplinary pain clinic, opioids may provide the only hope of relief to many sufferers of chronic pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
